/**
 * Every known moon of Earth, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn, as JPL lists them. Generated; do not edit by hand.
 *
 * Source (NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics, read 2026-10-18):
 * - Orbits: "Planetary Satellite Mean Elements", https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/sats/elem/ (every row for these planets).
 *   a = semi-major axis (km); frame L = the local Laplace plane (near the planet's equator), E = the ecliptic;
 *   i, node, w (argument of periapsis) and M (mean anomaly) in degrees at the table's epoch.
 * - Radii: "Planetary Satellite Physical Parameters", https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/sats/phys_par/ (mean radius, km; src P).
 *   Where that table has no row, the moon's own JPL Horizons physical data
 *   (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/api/horizons.api, OBJ_DATA) where it gives a radius (src H; a triaxial a x b x c is
 *   reduced to the volumetric mean (abc)^(1/3)). Where neither gives one, the radius is null: JPL publishes none.
 *
 * Columns: planet, name, JPL code, a (km), frame, i, node, w, M, radius (km) or null, radius source.
 */
export type MoonRow = [planet: 'earth' | 'mars' | 'jupiter' | 'saturn', name: string, code: number, aKm: number, frame: 'L' | 'E', i: number, node: number, w: number, M: number, radiusKm: number | null, src: 'P' | 'H' | ''];

